<title>CHINA: Nam Hing says yearly net doubled.</title>
<headline>Nam Hing says yearly net doubled.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   5.0	 vs  2.5</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    1.0	 vs  nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  6.28 gain vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    15.42     vs  7.01</p>
<p>    Turnover		     309.59    vs  309.52</p>
<p>    Company name		 Nam Hing Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 9-15</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 6</p>
<p>NOTE - Nam Hing makes laminates for electrical and electronic products. It also makes printed circuit boards and trades in raw materials and chemicals.</p>
<p>Exceptional gain is from sales of property.</p>
<p>The company proposes a bonus issue of one warrant for every five shares held. Each warrant, which expire on September 30, 1999, will entitle holders to the right to subscribe one new company share at HK$0.85 each subject to adjustment.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 2.0 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of one cent) vs two cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
